<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mysore Dasara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mysuru Dasara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> Dasara is the ten-day festival of Navaratri and Vijayadashami celebrated at Mysore in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the state festival of Karnataka. The Wodeyar kings continued the royal Mahanavami festival of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, beginning with Raja Wodeyar in 1610, to present themselves as its heirs. Its procession of decorated elephants carrying the image of the goddess Chamundeshwari still draws large crowds.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mysore-dasara.jpg" alt="Mysore Dasara" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ashwin Kumar from Bangalore, India · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mysore_Palace_Dussera_(29633564994).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
